  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="c0cc2264-0a02-5741-921a-96ad7f76268d" activityNameId="c65d4f7f-b113-57a1-890e-03148624a4fa" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Well for exploration and production, offshore</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Well for exploration and production, offshore
Process for all types of offshore drilling operations.;
4e467d03-a80f-37c4-a765-ad723cbd9def
All materials and emissions for drilling of an offshore bore hole and finishing of the well.  Not including energy, venting and flaring which is covered in general production data.
Location:  Data mainly found for GB and NO.
Technology: Drilling in the North Sea
Time period: Time of publication in literature and environmental reports. Most data are valid for the end of the 90ties.
Production volume: About 50km in NO and 100km in GB per year.
Sampling: Publication in environmental reports and other literature.
Extrapolations: Applied on all offshore drilling operations. There might be differences depending on depth of sea and type of geological formation
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4e467d03-a80f-37c4-a765-ad723cbd9def.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="3320dcee-ac7b-51fa-8397-bc03eb397f03" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">OCE</shortname>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Location:  Data mainly found for GB and NO.</text>
        </comment>
      </geography>
      <technology>
        <comment>
